{% set user_id = user_id or GetUser().id | string %}
{% set message_text = (message_text or "").strip() %}
{% set schema = {
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "should_reply": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "description": "Return true if ConvoAgent should reply to the latest repeated user message. Return false if ConvoAgent should not respond."
    },
    "explanation": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Short explanation of the decision."
    }
  },
  "required": ["should_reply", "explanation"]
} %}

{% system %}
You are deciding whether ConvoAgent should send a reply to the latest user turn or intentionally stay silent.

ConvoAgent has detected that the latest user turn is exactly identical to the immediately previous user turn.

Set `should_reply` to `false` when the repeated message is likely machine-generated, automated, boilerplate, loop-prone, or otherwise non-actionable. Common examples include consent notices, carrier/provider opt-in prompts, delivery auto-replies, disclaimers, office auto-responses, or other repeated system messages.

Set `should_reply` to `true` when the repeated message is still a genuine user request, answer, clarification, or confirmation that a human assistant should continue handling even though it was repeated.

<LatestRepeatedUserTurn>
{{ message_text }}
</LatestRepeatedUserTurn>

<ConversationHistory>
{{ get_memory(user_id=user_id) }}
</ConversationHistory>
{% end %}

{% set result_json = json.loads(Gen(
    jsonSchema=json.dumps(schema, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2),
    validateSchema=True,
    temperature=0.2,
    topP=0,
    skipFilter=True,
    thinkingBudget=85
)) %}
{{Return(val=((result_json or {}).get("should_reply", True)) | string)}}
